.TH tkusysinfo n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkusysinfo
.PP
A view of \fBtclutils::tusysinfo\fR: operating system, CPU, memory, computer model, disks and monitors as a tree, plus a "Screen" section from Tk itself (size in pixels and millimetres, DPI, \fBtk scaling\fR, colour depth, windowing system). Buttons: Refresh, Copy (text report to the clipboard), Save (text or JSON). Plain Tk (\fBttk::treeview\fR), no Tablelist.
.PP
Not in the \fBtkutils\fR umbrella: it needs \fBtclutils::tusysinfo\fR 0.1 from tclutils 0.69.0, while the umbrella still works with tclutils 0.64.0.
.CS
package require tkutils::tkusysinfo 0.1
.CE
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkusysinfo::widget .si ?options?]
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::refresh $w                 ;# collect again -> info dict
                                                  ;# an error shows "failed: …" in the status line
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::data    $w                 ;# last info dict
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::report  $w ?-anonymize 0|1? ;# text report
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::json    $w                 ;# JSON
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::save    $w file ?-format text|json? ?-anonymize 0|1?
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::screen  win                ;# Tk screen data as a dict
.CE
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-sections\fR	all	\fBtusysinfo\fR sections: \fBos cpu memory machine disks displays\fR
\fB\-serials\fR	\fB0\fR	\fB1\fR shows serial numbers
\fB\-timeout\fR	\fB10000\fR	limit in ms for one platform program
\fB\-autoload\fR	\fB1\fR	collect when the widget is built
\fB\-height\fR	\fB16\fR	visible rows
\fB\-buttons\fR	\fB1\fR	\fB0\fR hides the button bar
.TE
.PP
The info dict is the one from \fBtusysinfo::collect\fR with an extra key \fBscreen\fR. \fBreport\fR is \fBtusysinfo::report\fR plus a "Screen (Tk)" section; \fBjson\fR includes \fBscreen\fR.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require Tk
package require tkutils::tkusysinfo
pack [::tkutils::tkusysinfo::widget .si] -fill both -expand 1
.CE
.PP
Without the slow macOS \fBsystem_profiler\fR call:
.CS
::tkutils::tkusysinfo::widget .si -sections {os cpu memory}
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Tk sees one screen: with several monitors \fBpixels\fR is the whole desktop of the X screen (Linux) or the main monitor (Windows, macOS). The monitors themselves come from their EDID under "Monitors".
.IP \(bu
The two sections do not describe the same area. Example with two monitors under X11: Screen \fB3840x1200\fR (the whole desktop), Monitors BenQ \fBpreferred 3840x2560\fR (what the monitor can do), while it runs at 1920x1200 at +0+0. Running mode, position and primary monitor are in neither; the data does not tell on which monitor a window starts.
.IP \(bu
Collecting runs in the event loop of the caller; on macOS it takes a few seconds, the cursor shows \fBwatch\fR meanwhile.
.SS Errors
.PP
Unknown option: \fB{TKUTILS TKUSYSINFO OPTION <opt>}\fR with the known ones (\fBtkuopts\fR). Bad save format: \fB{TKUTILS TKUSYSINFO FORMAT}\fR. Errors of \fBtusysinfo\fR pass through.
